@startuml state-job-status
title State Machine - Job.status lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty description

[*] --> active : CreateJob (POST /company/jobs/create)

active --> paused : company TogglePauseJob\nor UpdateJob {status:"paused"}
paused --> active : company TogglePauseJob\nor UpdateJob {status:"active"}
active --> closed : admin CloseJob
paused --> closed : admin CloseJob
closed --> active : company UpdateJob {status:"active"}\n(permitted by code, see note)

active --> [*] : company DeleteJob / admin DeleteJob / company deleted
paused --> [*] : same deletions
closed --> [*] : same deletions

note right of closed
  TogglePauseJob explicitly rejects closed jobs
  (400 "This job was closed by the admin.").
  UpdateJob has no such check, so a company can send
  status "active" for a closed job. Observed in code;
  see implementation-gaps.md.
end note

note left of active
  Only "active" jobs are returned by GET /jobs and /jobs/latest,
  and only "active" jobs accept applications.
  Passing the deadline does NOT change status; ApplyJob checks
  the date, and the admin list derives a "Closed" label from daysLeft.
end note
@enduml
